<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#gallo-language">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gallo language</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gallo is a Romance language of the langue d'oïl group, spoken in eastern Brittany around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rennes">Rennes</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-malo">Saint-Malo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nantes">Nantes</a>. For centuries it was the everyday speech of Upper Brittany, while Breton, a Celtic language, prevailed in the west. Now spoken mainly by older people in the countryside, it is recognised by the region of Brittany as one of its languages.</p></div>
